---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import Todo from '../../components/Todo.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';
const o = site.operator;
---
<Base
  title="Privacy and terms"
  description="How Axarquía Home handles your personal data when you make a request, and who we share it with."
  path="/en/privacy/"
  lang="en"
>
  <Breadcrumbs lang="en" items={[{ name: 'Privacy and terms', href: '/en/privacy/' }]} />
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h1>Privacy and terms</h1>
      <Todo label="gegevens van de onderneming van Frans. Laat deze tekst één keer nakijken door een AVG-jurist." />
      <p>Last updated: 5 November 2026.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>The website {site.domain} is run by {o.name}, {o.address}, registered with the Netherlands Chamber of Commerce under number {o.kvk} (“Axarquía Home”). You can reach us at <a href={`mailto:${o.email}`}>{o.email}</a>.</p>
      <p>Axarquía Home does not carry out building work itself. Work is carried out by a carefully selected building company in the Axarquía that we work with (“the building company”). If you would like to know which company is handling your request, we will tell you on request.</p>

      <h2>What data we process</h2>
      <p>When you fill in our request form we process the information you give us: your name, email address, phone number, the address or town of the property, a description of your plans, your budget and timescale, and any photos. We also record the date and the page you made the request from.</p>

      <h2>Why, and on what legal basis</h2>
      <p>We only use this data to deal with your request: to call or email you, arrange a visit and prepare a quote. The legal basis is your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR), which you give by ticking the box on the form, and taking steps at your request before entering into a contract (Article 6(1)(b)).</p>

      <h2>Who we share your data with</h2>
      <p>Your request is automatically passed on to the building company, who will contact you and prepare the quote. If your request falls outside the building company’s work (for example solar panels or a removal), we only pass it on to one other partner if you have agreed to this on the form.</p>
      <p>Requests are stored in Axarquía Home’s Google Workspace (Google Sheets and Google Drive). Google processes this data on our behalf. We do not sell your data and do not use it for newsletters without your separate consent.</p>

      <h2>Free checklist and tips by email</h2>
      <p>If you request the free checklist, we keep your email address, your first name (if you give it), the stage you are at, your language and the page you signed up on. We use this to email you the checklist. If you also ticked the box for tips, we send you at most one email a week about buying, renovating and looking after a home in the Axarquía. You can withdraw that consent at any time through the unsubscribe link or by emailing {o.email}. A checklist sign-up is not passed on to the building company; that only happens if you make a request yourself. We keep this data until you unsubscribe, or for at most 24 months after your last contact with us.</p>

      <h2>How long we keep data</h2>
      <p>We keep requests for up to 24 months after our last contact, or longer where needed for the records of a contract (the statutory retention period for invoices in the Netherlands is 7 years).</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>You can ask us at any time which data we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, or withdraw your consent. Email <a href={`mailto:${o.email}`}>{o.email}</a>. You also have the right to complain to the Dutch Data Protection Authority (Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens), the Spanish Agencia Española de Protección de Datos or, if you live in the UK, the Information Commissioner’s Office.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and statistics</h2>
      <p>This website only places cookies if you agree to it in the cookie banner. We use Google Search Console and Bing Webmaster Tools to see how the site is found in search engines; nothing is stored on your device for this. We keep your choice in the banner in your browser (localStorage), so we do not ask on every page.</p>
      <p>To improve the website we use Microsoft Clarity. Clarity shows us how visitors use the pages, for example where they click and how far they scroll, through heatmaps and anonymous recordings of a visit. Clarity only loads if you click Accept in the cookie banner. It then places Microsoft cookies (such as _clck, _clsk and MUID) that are kept for up to a year. Anything you type into forms is masked. Microsoft processes this data on our behalf; see <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="noopener">Microsoft’s privacy statement</a>. The legal basis is your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR). You can withdraw it at any time through Cookie settings at the bottom of every page.</p>
      <p>We also use Google Analytics 4 to measure visits, for example how many people visit the site, which search engine they came from and which pages they read. Google Analytics also only loads if you click Accept in the cookie banner. It then places Google cookies (_ga and _ga_*) that are kept for up to two years. IP addresses are shortened and we do not share data for advertising. Google processes this data on our behalf; see <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google’s privacy policy</a>. The legal basis is your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR), which you can withdraw through Cookie settings at the bottom of every page.</p>

      <h2>Terms</h2>
      <p>The information on this website is general and has been prepared with care, but it is not legal, tax or building advice for your specific situation. Prices on the site are guide prices; only a written quote from the building company is binding. The building company is responsible for carrying out the work, guarantees and any complaints about the work.</p>
      <p>On legalisation (AFO) and permits we give general explanations only. The opinion on a specific property comes from an architect or lawyer.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
